1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:02,208
Monday, two in the afternoon.

2
00:00:02,258 --> 00:00:06,312
The keyholders are back at their desks, and Vault is open.

3
00:00:06,362 --> 00:00:10,320
In Lesson 38, three of them unsealed it.

4
00:00:10,370 --> 00:00:13,680
Now Timur installs everything else on top of it.

5
00:00:13,730 --> 00:00:22,416
Across town, Bekzod, the developer who connects Malika's toy shop to the bank, runs the same install on his laptop.

6
00:00:22,466 --> 00:00:26,328
This lesson is about why those two installs are the same.

7
00:00:26,378 --> 00:00:31,272
Elsewhere, someone installed the product by hand, and has since moved on.

8
00:00:31,322 --> 00:00:38,640
Months later, nobody knows which values production runs with, or why the test server behaves differently.

9
00:00:38,690 --> 00:00:43,632
An install nobody can repeat is an install nobody understands.

10
00:00:43,682 --> 00:00:50,264
So how can a laptop and a production server run the same install?

11
00:00:50,314 --> 00:00:55,064
So the steps are identical on a laptop, a test server and production.

12
00:00:55,114 --> 00:01:00,392
Only the values differ, and each environment's values are written down once.

13
00:01:00,442 --> 00:01:09,296
A value is anything that belongs to this bank in this place: an address, a certificate, an email for alerts.

14
00:01:09,346 --> 00:01:13,808
The card zone has its own values, and the bank sets every one.

15
00:01:13,858 --> 00:01:18,416
Who may call the card zone, and which roles each caller may use.

16
00:01:18,466 --> 00:01:28,760
The fraud limits from Lesson 14: how many refused tries a card, its first digits, an address or a shop may have within a window of time.

17
00:01:28,810 --> 00:01:35,312
How long a card entry session lives, how many tries it allows, and how long a code lives.

18
00:01:35,362 --> 00:01:37,664
Each is the bank's chosen value.

19
00:01:37,714 --> 00:01:40,784
Nothing has a default, and nothing is guessed.

20
00:01:40,834 --> 00:01:43,712
I think a default is a decision nobody made.

21
00:01:43,762 --> 00:01:48,848
The bank sets each value once for each environment, and they are kept in Vault.

22
00:01:48,898 --> 00:01:50,720
Order matters too.

23
00:01:50,770 --> 00:01:53,072
The card zone installs first.

24
00:01:53,122 --> 00:02:00,056
ecom then asks the card zone for its certificate, waits until it is signed, and carries on.

25
00:02:00,106 --> 00:02:03,872
Before anything is installed, a preflight runs.

26
00:02:03,922 --> 00:02:07,976
A preflight is a check of the machine before any work starts.

27
00:02:08,026 --> 00:02:12,776
It looks for what the install needs, such as the right tools and free ports.

28
00:02:12,826 --> 00:02:16,952
When something is missing, it says exactly what to fix.

29
00:02:17,002 --> 00:02:22,088
Then Vault is set up, and every service's settings are written from it.

30
00:02:22,138 --> 00:02:26,600
The services start in order, each one waiting for what it needs.

31
00:02:26,650 --> 00:02:34,232
A later change is just a new value, applied the same way, and only the services that use it restart.

32
00:02:34,282 --> 00:02:42,512
Every install ends with a health check: each service is asked whether it is ready, and answers a clear yes or no.

33
00:02:42,562 --> 00:02:46,880
Timur starts the card zone's installer on the fresh server.

34
00:02:46,930 --> 00:02:49,160
The preflight runs first.

35
00:02:49,210 --> 00:02:51,032
Most lines pass.

36
00:02:51,082 --> 00:02:54,728
One line fails, and right under it is the fix.

37
00:02:54,778 --> 00:02:57,200
Timur fixes it and starts again.

38
00:02:57,250 --> 00:02:59,072
Now everything passes.

39
00:02:59,122 --> 00:03:01,976
The installer asks for the release to run.

40
00:03:02,026 --> 00:03:05,048
Then it asks for the bank's values, one at a time.

41
00:03:05,098 --> 00:03:06,944
Where each door listens.

42
00:03:06,994 --> 00:03:09,368
Which callers may use the card zone.

43
00:03:09,418 --> 00:03:17,120
For each caller, the websites it serves, how long a card entry session lives, and how many tries it allows.

44
00:03:17,170 --> 00:03:20,072
Malika's shop is one of those websites.

45
00:03:20,122 --> 00:03:26,144
Then the fraud limits, the addresses for alerts, and the certificate for the payers' door.

46
00:03:26,194 --> 00:03:29,192
Every answer is checked as it is given.

47
00:03:29,242 --> 00:03:32,048
An answer in the wrong form is asked again.

48
00:03:32,098 --> 00:03:37,376
A certificate that does not match its key is asked again, with the reason.

49
00:03:37,426 --> 00:03:42,920
When every value is there, the installer says so, and how many it asked.

50
00:03:42,970 --> 00:03:49,520
It starts the services in order, and ends with the health check: every service healthy.

51
00:03:49,570 --> 00:03:52,784
Then Timur runs ecom's installer.

52
00:03:52,834 --> 00:03:58,208
It asks for its own values, sends its certificate request, and waits.

53
00:03:58,258 --> 00:04:01,328
On the card zone, the request is signed.

54
00:04:01,378 --> 00:04:06,560
ecom carries on, and its own health check shows every service healthy too.

55
00:04:06,610 --> 00:04:12,560
By evening, every value the bank runs on is written down, once, in one place.

56
00:04:12,610 --> 00:04:16,880
A missing value stops the install instead of being filled in.

57
00:04:16,930 --> 00:04:22,040
And what Bekzod tests on his laptop is the same install that runs in the bank.

58
00:04:22,090 --> 00:04:27,488
To recap: the steps are the same everywhere, and only the values differ.

59
00:04:27,538 --> 00:04:32,680
So what does the install do when a value is missing?

60
00:04:32,730 --> 00:04:35,056
It stops, and nothing is guessed.

61
00:04:35,106 --> 00:04:38,704
Next: how a release is numbered and shipped.
